    <system:String x:Key="Copilot.Tip">
        Tips: \n\n
        1. Before using, please confirm the job file matches your selected stage type.\n\n
        2. {key=Copilot.MainStage}, {key=Copilot.StoryCollection}, {key=Copilot.SideStory}: Please start from the screen where the blue "Start" button appears in the bottom right corner.\n\n
        3. {key=Copilot.SSS}: Multiple built-in files are in the resource/copilot folder. First create your squad manually, then start from the screen where the "Start Deployment" button appears in the bottom right. Can be used with ｢{key=Copilot.LoopTimes}｣.\n\n
        4. {key=Copilot.ParadoxSimulation}: After selecting Skills, start from the Skill selection screen where the "Start Simulation" button appears. For 1/2★ {key=Operator.Name}s (without Skills), start from the screen with the "Start Simulation" button in the bottom right. If using ｢{key=Copilot.UseCopilotList}｣, please start from the ｢Level/Rarity｣ tab in the {key=Operator.Name} list.\n\n
        5. {key=Operator.Name}s marked as "Favorite" may affect ｢{key=Copilot.AutoSquad}｣ recognition and selection. When using ｢{key=Copilot.AutoSquad}｣, consider removing favorites, or if errors occur, turn off ｢{key=Copilot.AutoSquad}｣ and manually supplement the missing {key=Operator.Name}s as prompted.\n\n
        6. ZOOT workstation codes can be pasted via the paste button on the right side of the input box. Formats are auto-detected:\n
        • prts://s = Job set prts:// = Single job\n\n
        7. {key=Copilot.UseCopilotList}:\n
        • After selecting a job, verify the stage name below is correct (e.g., CV-EX-1).\n
        • Add: Left-click for Normal difficulty, right-click for Challenge difficulty.\n
        • Clear: Left-click to clear all jobs, right-click to remove only inactive jobs.\n
        • Start from a screen where the target stage name is visible. Cross-chapter navigation is not supported.\n
        • Execution will stop automatically when sanity is insufficient, battle fails, or fails to achieve a 3★ clear.
    </system:String>
