    <system:String x:Key="Roguelike.ThemeTipBlackFlow" xml:space="preserve">{key=Roguelike.ThemeBlackFlow} recommended configuration:

{key=Settings.StartingCoreChar}: Mechanic (Elite 2 and the ｢Effect Improvement II｣ of the ｢Recruitment Mastery II｣ talent required)
{key=Settings.StartingSquad}: ｢{key=Settings.SpecialForceSquad}｣ / ｢{key=Settings.TacticalFortificationOperative}｣
{key=Settings.StartingRoles}: ｢{key=Settings.SlowAndSteadyWinsTheRace}｣ / ｢{key=Settings.Unbreakable}｣

1. There is no dedicated battle strategy yet; combat is decided automatically by the recruitment scoring system.
    Ingot farming and the fast flight to Floor 3 currently revolve around the Elite 2 Mechanic's flight.
    When starting with the setup above, once the Mechanic is recruited, the promotion check is skipped and the strategy runs as if it were Elite 2 for efficiency;
    when flying to Floor 3 quickly, a Mechanic without the full talent cannot fly, so an Elite 2 Mechanic with the full talent is required.
    Some events also have different options before the first clear and may get stuck; clearing N1 once satisfies both the Elite 2 requirement and the event options, and is fairly easy
2. You must unlock the ｢Effect Improvement II｣ of the ｢Recruitment Mastery II｣ talent, so that a ｢Structural Principle｣ part (fly anywhere on the map 3 times) is carried from the start.
    The unlock is easy — just sell 10 parts in total after Elite 2
3. Level farming only flies when ｢{key=Roguelike.BlackFlow.FastFlight}｣ is checked; the squad, roles and starting operator then switch to the setup above automatically.
    When unchecked, the run plays toward the target ending and does not fly even if it starts with the setup above. When farming starting rewards, the preparation run can also check ｢{key=Roguelike.BlackFlow.FastFlight}｣
4. Without an Elite 2 Mechanic with the full talent, you can still farm money normally, but battles will most likely end in defeat
5. Farming levels with ｢{key=Roguelike.BlackFlow.FastFlight}｣ checked and ｢{key=Roguelike.Investment.Enabled}｣ unchecked skips shops entirely</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Roguelike.ThemeTipJieGarden" xml:space="preserve">{key=Roguelike.ThemeJieGarden} recommended configuration:

{key=Settings.StartingSquad}: {key=Settings.LeaderSquad} / {key=Settings.TacticalRangedOperative}
{key=Settings.StartingRoles}: {key=Settings.SlowAndSteadyWinsTheRace}
{key=Settings.StartingCoreChar}: Wiš'adel

1. When the strategy is "Farm Originium Ingots", difficulty is ≥ N3 or "MAX", and {key=Settings.StartingSquad} is ｢{key=Settings.LeaderSquad}｣, the command-avoid-combat strategy will be enabled
2. The command-avoid-combat strategy greatly improves ingot farming efficiency and can also be used for quick leveling (without aiming to clear), but note the strategy must be set to "Farm Originium Ingots"
3. If the highest unlocked difficulty is &lt; N3 or the relevant tech is not unlocked, do not use the command-avoid-combat strategy; otherwise, it may cause errors
4. When difficulty ≥ N15, 6★ Hope cost +1; using some squads may make it impossible to recruit a 6★ operator at the start, causing errors or failures</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Roguelike.ThemeTipMizuki" xml:space="preserve">{key=Roguelike.ThemeMizuki} recommended configuration:

{key=Settings.StartingSquad}: {key=Roguelike.IS2.NewSquad3} / {key=Roguelike.IS2.NewSquad1}
