    <system:String x:Key="Schedule.WakeUp.Tip" xml:space="preserve">This feature registers scheduled tasks in Windows Task Scheduler to try to wake the computer and launch MAA 5 minutes before each enabled timer, after which the in-app scheduled start logic takes over.&#10;Auto-run items in ｢{key=Startup.Settings}｣ (e.g. {key=Settings.RunTaskAfterLaunch}, {key=Settings.OpenEmulatorAfterLaunch}) are skipped when launched by wake-up.&#10;The scheduled tasks remain after MAA exits and are removed when this switch is turned off.&#10;The keep-awake window only covers the wait before the task starts; for long-running tasks, enable ｢{key=Settings.BlockSleep}｣ in ｢{key=Settings.Game}｣ to prevent the system from sleeping during execution.&#10;Waking from hibernate depends on device firmware support; some devices only support waking from sleep.</system:String>
